Description:

The TLS session database is no longer synced to disk on every write.  It is
a cache, and losing writes only costs a client a full handshake.  With
http_allow_0rtt, which stores a session for every full handshake, this keeps
concurrent handshakes from queueing on each other's syncs.  twoskip, the
default tls_sessions_db backend, ignores the change and still syncs; twom
honours it.


Documentation:

The http_allow_0rtt entry in imapd.conf(5) now recommends keeping the session
database on fast storage, or in a backend such as twom.


Config changes:

None.


Upgrade instructions:

None.  Sites using http_allow_0rtt may want tls_sessions_db: twom, or
tls_sessions_db_path on tmpfs.


GitHub issue:

None.
